# Warn before live user impact

Match warnings to **who can see the site** and **what could touch reader progress or books**.

## Site tiers

**Owner-only** (basically only you): Maestro's (`/maestros/`), envDyst (`/envdyst/`), Climatic Mysteries (`/climatic-mysteries/`), CleanScreen (`/cleanscreen/`). Low reader risk.

**Public** (real readers): Halalit (`/halalit/`), Crocheter (`/crocheter/`), LoreKeeper (`/lorekeeper/` — account gate, quiet beta), HalaLyrics (`/halalyrics/`), oddtrove.art hub when served.

## Deploy check — always before running deploy

**Every time** deploy is about to run — including when the owner just said **deploy** / **deploy now** / **ship it** — give a short **Deploy check** **first**, then run the script **in the same turn** if they asked to deploy.

Do **not** run deploy silently. Do **not** skip the check because they said deploy.

**Deploy check** (plain English, 3–5 lines max):

1. **Verdict** — **Won't mess with readers** / **Minor blip only** / **May affect what readers see** (pick one; say why)
2. **What ships** — which site(s) and the kind of change (vet rules, copy, owner-only, accounts, etc.)
3. **Reader data** — shelves & Halalit progress on device **stay** unless you changed storage keys; Crocheter server sync called out if relevant
4. **If "May affect"** — one line on effect (e.g. Book Quest won't recommend X after refresh; Bookcheck shows new note; ~1–2s outage during restart)

Then deploy (if they asked) or ask **deploy now or local only?** (if they didn't).

### High-impact changes (usually "May affect what readers see")

- Halalit vetting & shelf rules — `halalit-curated-shelf-warnings.js`, `halalit-family-shelf-policy.js`, `halalit-bookquest-age-ratings.js`, Book Quest rec lists
- Reader progress & saves — localStorage keys, Book Quest state, import/series logic, Crocheter sync keys
- Accounts — Crocheter / LoreKeeper auth, sign-up toggles, `/api/auth/`
- Routes, deleted pages, nginx, auth gates
- LoreKeeper notes/docs storage keys or account isolation

**Halalit vet deploy:** personal shelves **not wiped**; recommendations & Bookcheck **do** update after refresh; cover clicks on existing shelf **fine**; brief restart blip possible.

### Usually "Minor blip only" or "Won't mess"

- Owner-only `www/` changes (Maestro's, envDyst, Climatic Mysteries — no public paths in the rsync set)
- Public copy/CSS/layout with no shelf/vet/progress/account changes
- Roster markdown only with no `halalit/www/` change → **no deploy needed**; say so

## When owner did NOT ask to deploy

- **Public** changes — do not deploy. Give Deploy check if relevant, then ask **deploy now or local only?**
- **Owner-only** changes (Maestro's, envDyst, Climatic Mysteries) — follow **`owner-only-auto-deploy`**: verify, brief deploy check, deploy in the same turn without asking.

## When owner said "local only" / "don't deploy"

No deploy for the rest of the conversation unless they later say deploy.

## Safe without Deploy check

- Edits that stay local (no deploy)
- Private files only (`halalit/.cursor/private/`, roadmap, My TBR)
